┌───────────────────────────────┐
│   1. How to build             │
└───────────────────────────────┘

Prepare for FindWayland.cmake (NOT NEEDED ANYMORE)
 $ sudo apt install extra-cmake-modules

Prepare SDL3
 clone the git repo and place it in `extern/SDL`
 install the development headers of liburing (e.g. liburing-dev on Ubuntu)

Prepare hwloc
 clone the git repo and place it in `extern/hwloc`
 Do we need to libpciaccess and/or libudev? Probably?

Configure cmake build
 $ CC=clang-21 cmake -B build-Debug -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -G Ninja
 $ CC=clang-21 cmake -B build-RelWithDebInfo -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -G Ninja
 $ CC=clang-21 cmake -B build-ship_it -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -G Ninja

Start building
 $ time cmake --build build-RelWithDebInfo

You can get the list of the compile commands and use it for auto-complete or other useful tools.
 $ ln -s build-RelWithDebInfo/compile_commands.json .

I'm getting used to debugging tools
 $ valgrind --track-origins=yes --leak-check=yes build-RelWithDebInfo/RelWithDebInfo/carbonara 
 $ build-Debug/Debug/carbonara
 $ build-RelWithDebInfo/RelWithDebInfo/carbonara
